Review the uncommitted stmap14 AutoEDA iteration in this ABC repository.

Focus on correctness and regression risk. The intended hypothesis is:
stmap14 keeps stmap13 guard-stat instrumentation and stmap12 lower-moderate
middle-slack bucket selection, but tightens middle-slack relief by requiring a
candidate exact-area match to save two inverter areas instead of one.

Expected implementation shape:
- New command file: src/base/abci/abcStmap_14.c
- Registration/build integration: src/base/abci/abc.c, src/base/abci/module.make, abclib.dsp
- Mapper mode: fSkipFanout == 15 in src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c
- Guard-stat print supports mode 14 as stmap13 and mode 15 as stmap14 in src/map/mapper/mapperCore.c
- Existing stmap0 through stmap13 behavior should remain buildable and comparable.

Validation already run before this review:
- make ABC_USE_NO_READLINE=1
- ./abc -c "stmap14 -h"
- smoke flow on benchmarks/i10.aig
- full baseline/candidate flow on all four required benchmarks
- guard-stat parsing
- CEC on all four required benchmarks

Artifacts are under .autoeda/runtime/results/stmap14/.
Please report findings by severity with file/line references, and distinguish source-code findings from required post-review logging/state updates.


