.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:- next-step recommendation: `stmap12` keeps final delay wins on all four benchmarks and improves `syn2` delay relative to `stmap11`, but it gives back `ode` delay and increases `syn2` area. For `stmap13`, add guard-hit counters or a lower-moderate bucket sub-split that distinguishes `syn2` timing-positive choices from area-expensive downstream sizing choices, preferably logging per-bucket hit counts before changing another threshold.
.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:## version13 / stmap13
.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:- motivation: `stmap12` preserved final delay wins on all four benchmarks, but it gave back `ode` delay and increased `syn2` area. The prior recommendation was to record guard-hit counters before tuning the lower-moderate bucket further. `stmap13` is an instrumentation-first version that keeps mapper behavior comparable to `stmap12`.
.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:- command name: `stmap13`
.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:  - `.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap13/*`
.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:- algorithm summary: `stmap13` keeps the classic `map` SCL genlib gain default of `250` and passes `fSkipFanout = 14` into the mapper. `mapperMatch.c` treats mode `14` as the same decision policy as `stmap12` mode `13`: delay matching and small-graph/area-flow behavior match the existing shape-gated fanout guard, and exact-area recovery on larger graphs allows the tight-depth one-to-two inverter slack area-relief bypass only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. Mode `14` additionally records exact-area risky-cut, fanout-bucket, middle-slack, relief, and rejection counters; `mapperCore.c` prints one `stmap13 guard stats` line after mapping. Existing `map` and `stmap0` through `stmap12` behavior are preserved because modes `0` through `13` retain their prior meanings.
.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:  - build: `make ABC_USE_NO_READLINE=1` passed; artifact `./abc` produced. Log: `.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap13/build.log`.
.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:  - help: `./abc -c "stmap13 -h"` printed usage text with default `-G 250.00` and the stmap12 guard counters enabled. Log: `.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap13/help.log`.
.autoeda/runtime/versions.md:  - smoke: `read_lib 7nm_lvt_ff.lib; read benchmarks/i10.aig; resyn; resyn2; dch -v; stmap13; topo; buffer; upsize -v; dnsize -v; stime` passed with final delay `198.64 ps` and area `1303.10`. Log: `.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap13/smoke_i10.log`.
